          "schemaValid": false
        }
      ],
      "conformance": [
        "tests/unit/test_media_geospatial.py",
        "tests/unit/test_ffmpeg_video_input.py",
        "tests/unit/test_ffmpeg_allocation.py",
        "tests/unit/test_ffmpeg_h264_readback.py",
        "tests/unit/test_ffmpeg_review.py",
        "tests/unit/test_ffmpeg_audio.py"
      ],
      "acceptance": [
        "tools/qualify_media_geospatial.py",
        "tools/qualify_ffmpeg_deliverable.py",
        "tools/qualify_ffmpeg_video.py",
        "tools/qualify_ffmpeg_review.py",
        "tools/qualify_ffmpeg_audio.py"
      ],
      "profiles": {
        "workflow": {
          "scope": "Consumes image, spriteSheet, spriteMetadata and bounded MP4/H264 or Matroska/FFV1 video artifacts, plus file artifacts (SoX WAV, whisper.cpp SRT; one limited native chain on a single clip, not a corpus) for muxReview; fixed output rate, no automatic conversion. Existing operations publish silent video; muxReview publishes a three-stream review movie. extractAudio consumes one MP4/M4A file artifact and publishes a canonical PCM16 WAV file artifact (handed to SoX conform in ffmpeg-extract-audio-workflow.json; one bounded chain, not a corpus).",
          "references": [
            "docs/media-workflows.md#ffmpeg-publication",
            "tests/unit/test_media_geospatial.py",
            "docs/ffmpeg.md"
          ]
        },
        "composition": {
          "scope": "Shared document references, pure value functions and expressions resolve for every finite analytic visit before native validation.",
          "references": [
            "docs/adaptor-runtime.md",
            "tests/unit/test_adaptor_runtime.py"
          ]
        }
      },
      "development": {
        "api": [
          "https://ffmpeg.org/ffmpeg.html",
          "https://ffmpeg.org/ffprobe.html"
        ],
        "lifecycle": {
          "timeout": "Native encoding and decoding use a shared elapsed-time budget.",
          "cancellation": "Owned native subprocess trees use shared cancellation and retain partial evidence.",
          "logs": "Retain stage stdout/stderr, commands, probe output, decoded RGB and submissions.",
          "verification": "Recheck full decoded RGB against retained inputs, dimensions, count, duration, hashes and declared codec-dependent error limits. Authored deliverable acceptance is reconstructed from native duration, dimensions/count, actual compressed byte size and per-frame mean RGB errors; unmet results cannot be published as successes. New native decode/probe launchers bind the encoded input digest to each owned stage; launcher source, bindings and decoded/probe output digests are replayed offline. Historical direct commands remain explicitly unbound. Verification of encodeFrames, encodeSheet and encodeVideo, standalone and at the end of a run, decodes and probes private copies of the held published bytes (and, for encodeVideo, the held captured source video) again with a trusted FFmpeg and sibling ffprobe (explicit executable, stored configuration or FFMPEG_EXECUTABLE; never receipt paths or PATH) under the shared deadline, cancellation and byte limits, then judges every frame, the frame order and count, dimensions, cadence, codec, declared colour tags and fidelity budget against the captured PNG pixels or the fresh source decode; retained readbacks, receipt and result are strict typed consistency checks only, and a contradiction is VERIFICATION_FAILED with observed.fresh true. muxReview verification additionally decodes the published review file and the captured video again with a trusted FFmpeg and sibling ffprobe (explicit executable, stored configuration or FFMPEG_EXECUTABLE; never receipt paths or PATH) in a private directory under the shared deadline and cancellation, derives expectations from the captured sources, parses retained JSON strictly with typed comparison and requires result.json to equal the verified outcome; a bare schemaxis verify needs the stored configuration or environment variable. Source capture and scheduler fingerprints reject non-regular inputs before opening and recheck descriptors, with bounded byte reads. Existing video sources retain every decoded frame plus captured compressed bytes; bound source probe/decode launchers and full-source cadence validation precede pure index slicing. Native source processes have POSIX memory/file caps; all stages share one timeout. muxReview: every output stage (mux, probe, video decode, audio decode, caption extraction) is bound by an adaptor-owned launcher to the digests of the exact files it opens; verification is host re-derivation plus a fresh native decode: the host re-derives the strict WAV/SRT parse, the exact rational duration policy and every comparison from captured sources and retained readbacks, and the published review file and captured video are also decoded again with a trusted FFmpeg (as described above), so changed captured sources, published bytes or readbacks are rejected even when ordinary publication hashes are refreshed. extractAudio: the captured MP4/M4A bytes are held once; a fresh private copy is probed (streams, format, chapters, programs) and its selected audio-frame timeline listed (contiguous timestamps from zero, bounded count) by a trusted FFmpeg and sibling ffprobe (explicit executable, stored configuration or FFMPEG_EXECUTABLE; never PATH or receipt paths) under the shared deadline and cancellation, with POSIX address-space, CPU, file-size and core caps, then decoded to PCM16 with fixed arguments; the host builds the 44-byte canonical WAV and requires every PCM byte of the fresh decode to equal the published WAV, the decoded frame count to equal the probed audio-frame total, and the summary, receipt and result (closed, typed) to equal the recomputed observation. The capture is an unauthenticated trust anchor and AAC is lossy; no equality to the original recording, recognition accuracy or human review is claimed. extractAudio native stages report faults by cause: a stage that reaches its output cap (probe output over 4 MiB, a decode larger than the counted frames) is RESOURCE_LIMIT before any source diagnostic is read; native source diagnostics are INVALID_RESOURCE; loader, allocation, unclassified or empty-output failures are RUNNER_FAILED (source validity not established); during verification each becomes VERIFICATION_FAILED with the cause retained and observed.fresh set."
        },
        "data": [
          {
            "id": "frames",
            "direction": "input",
            "kind": "image",
            "format": "PNG",
            "traits": {
              "colour": "8-bit RGB/RGBA",
              "order": "explicit",
              "units": "pixels"
            },
            "losses": [
              "Alpha composites on black."
            ],
            "scope": "Equal dimensions and bounded non-interlaced PNG subset."
          },
          {
            "id": "sheet",
            "direction": "input",
            "kind": "spriteSheet",
            "format": "PNG",
            "traits": {
              "colour": "8-bit RGB/RGBA",
              "order": "metadata rectangles"
            },
            "losses": [
              "Alpha composites on black."
            ],
            "scope": "Sheet needs matching metadata."
          },
          {
            "id": "metadata",
            "direction": "input",
            "kind": "spriteMetadata",
            "format": "schemaxis.aseprite.sheet/1",
            "traits": {
              "order": "authored",
              "timeUnits": "milliseconds"
            },
            "losses": [
              "Frame duration must be representable at the chosen constant fps."
            ],
            "scope": "Explicit rectangles and durations."
          },
          {
            "id": "video",
            "direction": "output",
            "kind": "video",
            "format": "MP4/H.264 or Matroska/FFV1",
            "traits": {
              "frameRate": "constant",
              "audio": false,
              "colour": "RGB decode"
            },
            "losses": [
              "H.264 is lossy; FFV1 is byte-exact after alpha compositing."
            ],
            "scope": "No colour-management guarantee."
          },
          {
            "id": "source-video",
            "direction": "input",
            "kind": "video",
            "format": "MP4/H.264 yuv420p or Matroska/FFV1 bgr0",
            "traits": {
              "frameIndices": "zero-based presentation frames, inclusive start/exclusive end",
              "frameRate": "integer constant source rate; output fps retimes selection",
              "audio": false
            },
            "losses": [
              "FFV1 output preserves source decoded RGB, not pre-compression source colours.",
              "No colour-management guarantee; non-square pixels, rotation/side data and interlacing rejected."
            ],
            "scope": "Exactly one video stream, <=600 frames,32 MiB compressed,192 MiB RGB; fixed local demuxers; default MP4 edit-list presentation is honoured."
          },
          {
            "id": "source-audio",
            "direction": "input",
            "kind": "file",
            "format": "PCM16 WAV (canonical fmt+data)",
            "traits": {
              "channels": "mono or stereo",
              "sampleRate": "8000-96000 Hz",
              "units": "PCM sample frames"
            },
            "losses": [
              "Copied unchanged; never trimmed, padded or resampled."
            ],
            "scope": "muxReview audio, up to 32 MiB; duration within one video frame period of the video."
          },
          {
            "id": "source-captions",
            "direction": "input",
            "kind": "file",
            "format": "SubRip (UTF-8, plain text)",
            "traits": {
              "timeUnits": "milliseconds",
              "order": "contiguous monotonic cues"
            },
            "losses": [
              "Plain text only; markup and positioning are rejected, never converted."
            ],
            "scope": "muxReview captions, up to 1000 cues and 256 KiB; machine-draft status is declared, never verified."
          },
          {
            "id": "review-movie",
            "direction": "output",
            "kind": "video",
            "format": "Matroska FFV1 + PCM16 + SubRip",
            "traits": {
              "streams": "video, audio, subtitle",
              "captions": "soft",
              "burnIn": false
            },
            "losses": [
              "No re-encoding; no metadata, chapters, attachments or fonts."
            ],
            "scope": "Exactly three streams; decoded content independently compared with the captured sources."
          },
          {
            "id": "source-aac",
            "direction": "input",
            "kind": "file",
            "format": "MP4/M4A with one AAC-LC audio stream (optionally one H.264 video stream)",
            "traits": {
              "channels": "mono or stereo",
              "sampleRate": "standard AAC rates 8000-96000 Hz",
              "streamIndex": "global index 0-15, authored",
              "units": "PCM sample frames after decode"
            },
            "losses": [
              "AAC is lossy; the decoded PCM is not the recording that was encoded.",
              "Video, metadata, chapters, cover art and every other stream are dropped; extra audio, subtitle, data and cover-art streams are refused."
            ],
            "scope": "extractAudio: <=64 MiB compressed, <=600 s, canonical WAV <=32 MiB; intact, non-fragmented, self-contained MP4 under a forced mov demuxer and file protocol only."
          },
          {
            "id": "extracted-audio",
            "direction": "output",
            "kind": "file",
            "format": "PCM16 WAV (canonical 44-byte header)",
            "traits": {
              "channels": "source mono or stereo",
              "sampleRate": "source rate, no resampling",
              "units": "PCM sample frames",
              "status": "machineDraft"
            },
            "losses": [
              "Lossy AAC decode; no equality with the uncompressed original, no recognition accuracy and no human review is certified."
            ],
            "scope": "audio.wav plus audio-summary.json (codec, stream index, decoded geometry, duration, PCM digest); accepted by the SoX conform route and muxReview."
          }
        ],
        "inspection": [
          {
            "panel": "text",
            "scope": "Inspect retained probe and verification JSON.",
            "limits": "Video playback is external; the shared console does not advertise a video player."
          }
        ],
        "authoring": {
          "model": "nodes",
          "example": "video-range",
          "reuse": "Bind a captured source video; select startFrame inclusive/endFrame exclusive and choose output fps to retime. Changes to source bytes invalidate scheduler reuse; replan and run into a fresh directory."
        },
        "features": {
          "workflow": {
            "status": "supported",
            "scope": "Declared artifact receipts, scheduler provenance and explicit handoffs; verify each consumer format."
          },
          "native-inspection": {
            "status": "unsupported",
            "scope": "Inspect retained publications and receipts; no native node inspection hook is advertised."
          },
          "composition": {
            "status": "supported",
            "scope": "Shared document references, pure value functions and expressions resolve for every finite analytic visit before native validation."
          },
          "mpi": {
            "status": "unsupported",
            "scope": "Only serial execution is qualified; do not request multiple ranks."
          },
          "reusable-inputs": {
            "status": "supported",
            "scope": "The registered hook hashes external inputs for scheduler reuse."
          },
          "time-batches": {
            "status": "unsupported",
            "scope": "No finite native time-list batching support in this route."
          },
          "source-authoring": {
            "status": "supported",
            "scope": "Edit ordinary JSON through the shared draft source; planning checks the current revision."
          },
          "property-authoring": {
            "status": "supported",
            "scope": "Use atomic JSON pointer patches through the shared draft model; node commands apply only to node-shaped routes."
          },
          "live-editing": {
            "status": "unsupported",
            "scope": "Use bounded batch execution; no persistent native editing session is promised."
          },
          "native-save": {
            "status": "unsupported",
            "scope": "Inspect and reuse declared publications; no console native-save extension is advertised for this route."
          },
          "conversion": {
            "status": "supported",
            "scope": "Explicit PNG/sprite-sheet or bounded existing-video frame-range conversion to silent H.264/FFV1; FFV1 preserves decoded source RGB, H.264 is lossy. No automatic conversion planning. muxReview additionally muxes verified FFV1 video, PCM16 audio and SubRip captions without re-encoding. extractAudio decodes one AAC-LC audio stream of an MP4/M4A to a canonical PCM16 WAV and summary, verified by a fresh native decode."
          }
        },
        "cases": [
          {
            "id": "frames-baseline",
            "example": "ordered-frames",
            "edits": [],
            "scope": "One known PNG encoded as FFV1 at 25 fps; independently decoded RGB must be byte-exact after alpha compositing. Does not qualify H.264 or sprite timing.",
            "checks": [
              {
                "file": "verification.json",
                "format": "json",
                "pointer": "/frames",
                "expected": 1
              },
              {
                "file": "verification.json",
                "format": "json",
                "pointer": "/fps",
                "expected": 25
              },
              {
                "file": "verification.json",
                "format": "json",
                "pointer": "/meanErrors",
                "expected": [
                  0.0
                ]
              }
            ],
            "resources": {
              "/nodes/0/options/files/0": "examples/schemaxis/catalogue-texture.png"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "frames-variant",
            "example": "ordered-frames",
            "edits": [
              {
                "op": "add",
                "path": "/nodes/0/options/fps",
                "value": 12
              }
            ],
            "scope": "One known PNG encoded as FFV1 at 12 fps; independently decoded RGB must be byte-exact after alpha compositing. Does not qualify H.264 or sprite timing.",
            "checks": [
              {
                "file": "verification.json",
                "format": "json",
